+#ifdef SQLITE_ENABLE_WAL2_COREAD
+/*
+** WAL2 co-located read (experimental scaffold). See the WalCoRead comment
+** near the WalIndexHdr definition. These let K connections latch the SAME
+** wal2 frame an anchor read-transaction already holds, WITHOUT the general
+** sqlite3_snapshot machinery (which is disabled in wal2 mode). Correctness
+** rests on: (1) the caller keeps the anchor read transaction OPEN for the
+** lifetime of every co-located reader, so the anchor's read-lock protects
+** these frames against reset; (2) the fail-closed walCoReadStillValid()
+** check. NOT production-ready: validity is salt-only -- prove with the
+** corruption-test gauntlet before enabling on a real replica.
